{
  "category": "Sludge Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "Thickly covered with a filthy, vile sludge. It is so toxic, even its footprints contain poison.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thickly covered with a filthy, vile sludge. It is so toxic, even its footprints contain poison.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration, it lost its sense of smell.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "They love to gather in smelly areas where sludge ac cumulates, making the stench around them worse.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is made of a powerful poison. Touching it accidentally will cause a fever that requires bed rest.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "As it moves, a very strong poison leaks from it, making the ground there barren for three years.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "From MUK’s body seeps a foul fluid that gives off a nose-bendingly horrible stench. Just one drop of this POKéMON’s body fluid can turn a pool stagnant and rancid.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "This POKéMON’s favorite food is anything that is repugnantly filthy. In dirty towns where people think nothing of throwing away litter on the streets, MUK are certain to gather.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "It prefers warm and humid habitats. In the summertime, the toxic substances in its body intensify, making MUK reek like putrid kitchen garbage.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "It is usually undetectable because it blends in with the ground. Touching it can cause terrible poisoning.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "Thickly covered with a filthy, vile sludge. It is so toxic, even its footprints contain poison.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "They love to gather in smelly areas where sludge accumulates, making the stench around them worse.",
      "version": "heartgold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is made of a powerful poison. Touching it accidentally will cause a fever that requires bed rest.",
      "version": "soulsilver"
    },
    {
      "text": "A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s so stinky! Muk’s body contains toxic elements, and any plant will wilt when it passes by.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "It’s so stinky! Muk’s body contains toxic elements, and any plant will wilt when it passes by.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "They love to gather in smelly areas where sludge accumulates, making the stench around them worse.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "A toxic fluid seeps from its body. The fluid instantly kills plants and trees on contact.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "From Muk’s body seeps a foul fluid that gives off a nose-bendingly horrible stench. Just one drop of this Pokémon’s body fluid can turn a pool stagnant and rancid.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "This Pokémon’s favorite food is anything that is repugnantly filthy. In dirty towns where people think nothing of throwing away litter on the streets, Muk are certain to gather.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "The stench it gives off will make your nose scrunch up. Still, there are Muk fans who think that’s a good thing.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "After recent environmental improvements, this Pokémon is now hardly seen at all. People speculate that it may go extinct at some point.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Their food sources have decreased, and their numbers have declined sharply. Sludge ponds are being built to prevent their extinction.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Because they scatter germs everywhere, they’ve long been targeted for extermination, leading to a steep decline in their population.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration of its nose, it lost its sense of smell.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "Smells so awful, it can cause fainting. Through degeneration of its nose, it lost its sense of smell.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    }
